package santa

// Authored eval + wire vectors for sigma-rust's santa-probe-method-call-static-type (fork PR 95, from its vector
// backlog, 2026-11-14). Measured first in santa.spike.StaticTypeProbe (local).
//
// THE RULE, read in 6.0.7: `applySubst` (sigma/ast/package.scala:72-81) has TWO regimes. A function type handed to it
// directly DROPS the type parameters the substitution names; any other type is rewritten bottom-up by kiama, which
// walks into a nested function type's `STypeParam`, renames a parameter whose variable becomes another variable, and
// THROWS (`dup illegal arguments`) when it becomes a type. A type a script wrote meets it three times while a call
// is parsed: the explicit type argument's substitution, `specializeFor`'s (SMethod.scala:193-199), and
// `MethodCall.tpe`'s SECOND application of the explicit substitution (values.scala:1355-1358), which changes the
// call's type wherever the range still names the method's `T` (`getReg[Coll[T]](4)` is an `Option[Coll[Coll[T]]]`).
// It concerns the six methods with an explicit type argument, all at tree v3: Box.getReg, Context.getVarFromInput,
// Global.deserializeTo, fromBigEndianBytes, some, none. An implementation that substitutes once, or without the
// throw, parses trees the JVM rejects (also in a branch never taken), refuses trees the JVM parses, and types the
// node around the call otherwise.
//
// EVERY PARSE ROW is wrapped as `if (true) true else { val v = <expr>; false }`: the expression parses exactly as it
// does alone (nothing around it checks its type), the tree evaluates to `true` when it is built and errors when it
// is refused, and a lenient implementation cannot hide behind a root it cannot write (sigma-rust's roots are bare:
// an `Option` of a lambda, say). The evaluation rows (a value or a throw at evaluation) stay as sigma-rust wrote them.
// CONTROLS: up to four PARSING rows per method group from each of sigma-rust's full sets, and its reviewer's parsing
// rows-r2 rows, less the ones on the Coll and Option method tables (the method_type_variable_names families hold those).
//
// Families: eval MethodCall.static_type_substitution_v6 (activated 3, tree v3); wire
// ErgoTree.static_type_substitution (v6: the whole sized trees, each REJECTED: kiama's RuntimeException is no
// ValidationException, so nothing degrades). Left out: the growth tree (a parse blow-up in a port that copies the
// type; it wants a time bound SANTA has no grading for: on the taskboard as a design decision).

